Given a set of bounds `B`, expands to the function:

```ignore (pseudo-rust)
fn(min) -> bool {
    exists (b in B) { b(min) }
}
```

In other words, if we meet some bound in `B`, that suffices.
This is used when all the bounds in `B` are known to apply to `G`.
